; case: addressable-region
; verdict: accept
; ambiguous: yes
; tests: externality=pass implementation-independence=pass non-prescription=pass
; rationale: AMBIGUOUS, resolved ACCEPT. A concrete address range reads like a driver detail,
;   yet it is an externally relevant platform fact: it constrains placement, aliasing and
;   ownership regardless of which driver is chosen. §4.3 is explicit that "a concrete
;   architectural identity or addressable region may legitimately constrain a platform". The
;   limit is equally explicit: this is not permission to put the region's *access procedure*
;   in the language — see the rejected case `register-programming-sequence`.
; other-side: engine: the register map within the region, access widths, the driver, and the
;   safe API over it
;
(eadl-version eadl/1)

(defplatform soc.memory
  (offers
    (region device.timer
      (base 0x1000_0000)
      (size 64 KiB)
      (reserved true))))
